{"term":"van","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:72ca59b37a1745d1ea","definition":"A covered motor vehicle used to carry goods or (normally less than ten) persons, usually roughly cuboid in shape, Depending on the type of van, it can be bigger or smaller than a pickup truck and SUV, and longer and higher than a car but relatively smaller than a truck/lorry or a bus.","example":"While Santa Monica has a longstanding prohibition against public camping that includes living in vehicles, the van rental business has been a problem in Venice for years. […] Organizations that provide safe parking locations have limited capacity and are often unable to accommodate the kind of non-operational vans that are being repurposed as makeshift housing.","pos":"noun","synonyms":["minivan","minibus"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["armored van","baggage van","box van","brake van","campervan","camper van","car-body van","conversion van","cube van","delivery van","detector van","devan","divvy van","dollar van","driving van trailer","e-van","ferry van","gas van","goods van","guard's van","hoolivan","ice cream van","loony van","luggage van","Luton van","mailvan","microvan","motor-van","moving van","newsvan"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/van#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:ebb7e1ad8e4e66fc0f","definition":"An enclosed railway vehicle for transport of goods, such as a boxcar/box van.","example":"","pos":"noun","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"UK","register":"UK","wordFamily":["armored van","baggage van","box van","brake van","campervan","camper van","car-body van","conversion van","cube van","delivery van","detector van","devan","divvy van","dollar van","driving van trailer","e-van","ferry van","gas van","goods van","guard's van","hoolivan","ice cream van","loony van","luggage van","Luton van","mailvan","microvan","mot